Falsifies `globally_unique_identifier_partition_table::verification::a_span_always_contains_what_was_asked_for`.

The defect: the check that the span's end still names a block is gone, so a range near the top of
a 64-bit disk gets a span whose first block plus its length passes `u64::MAX`. A caller that adds
them to find the end wraps around to the start of the disk.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(u128::from(s.first_block) + u128::from(s.blocks) <= u128::from(u64::MAX))`,
on an offset in the last block of the address space with a length that reaches past it.
